            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A gas barrier laminate (10) of the present invention includes a biaxially-oriented polypropylene base (1) and an aluminum oxide thin film (2) formed on one surface of the biaxially-oriented polypropylene base (1). The biaxially-oriented polypropylene base (1) has a plane orientation factor ΔP ranging from 0.005 to 0.020 according to phase-contrast measurement and the aluminum oxide thin film shows a ratio of oxygen and aluminum (O/AI) ranging from 1.0 to 1.5 as calculated by X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy. The biaxially-oriented polypropylene base is provided, on the one surface thereof, with a primer-treated layer (4) formed by discharge treatment.</p>
            </abstract>
